# double) become one token each, with one layer of quoting stripped --
# this is what keeps a push phrase inside a multi-word quoted literal, or
# a heredoc body, from ever being scanned as shell tokens: heredoc bodies
# are skipped by line entirely (never fed into the token loop at all), and
# a quoted interior becomes exactly one token regardless of what words it
# contains. && and || are two-char operators; ; | ( ) and newline are
# one-char operators; everything else is whitespace-delimited.
